  "body": "### Summary\nAs an iPad user browsing Catégories in landscape (regular width), I want a sub-forum chosen in the « Sous-forum » picker to load its topics, so that I can read it. Today the column shows the sub-forum's name over an empty list.\n\n### Facts (runtime pass of #1388, mac/mac-mbp, simulator iPad Pro 13\", iOS 27.2)\n- Scenario 3 of #1388 on iPad: category → « Sous-forum » picker → a sub-forum. The trace shows the category list's `onAppear`, the picker's `scope.select`, then **no** `topicList.task`, no load and no request for the sub-forum for 25 s (`list forum onAppear start` at 4315 ms, `open subforum` at 9334 ms, wait timed out at 34518 ms).\n- Suspected cause (by reading, `dev-swift` @ `1685bcc1`): in `App/SwiftHFR/Root/RootSidebarView.swift` (~:224-231, `CategoriesSidebarColumn`), the `TopicListView` inside `navigationDestination(item: $navigation.selectedSource)` has no `.id(source)`, while the compact `TopicsColumn` in `RootTabsView.swift` (~:191) has one; so the new model's `.task(id: model.wantedFilter)` never runs.\n- Caveat: driven by a scratch autopilot through the same `scope.select` the picker calls; confirm by hand on an iPad.\n\n### Scope\n- `.id(source)` (or the equivalent) on that `TopicListView`; check the other sidebar columns for the same pattern.\n- A hosted iPad-sidebar test where selecting a sub-forum loads its list (red first).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- On iPad regular width, choosing a sub-forum loads its first page; the compact path is unchanged.\n\nFound by the #1388 runtime pass (N1). Refs #1388, #774.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
